{"comments":[{"id":"IC_kwDOKFU0lc8AAAABdaw8Gw","author":{"login":"github-actions"},"authorAssociation":"CONTRIBUTOR","body":"<!-- require-issue-link -->\n**This PR has been automatically closed** because you are not assigned to the linked issue.\n\nExternal contributors must be assigned to an issue before opening a PR for it. Please:\n1. Comment on the linked issue to request assignment from a maintainer\n2. Once assigned, your PR will be reopened automatically\n\n*Maintainers: reopen this PR or remove the `missing-issue-link` label to bypass this check.*","createdAt":"2026-10-19T14:07:56Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/pull/9352#issuecomment-6269189147","viewerDidAuthor":false},{"id":"IC_kwDOKFU0lc8AAAABgVAILA","author":{"login":"flyoung588"},"authorAssociation":"NONE","body":"@JohnnyWilson16 I followed up on the custom-init/defaulted-alias regression from #9343 with a load-only repair prototype and additional compatibility checks (AI-assisted execution).\n\n[Pinned patch, runnable tests and raw outputs](https://github.com/flyoung588/recursive-productive-capacity/tree/b64d0d90e1e6ff42956b5aa847571cb763cbd7a6/co-do-003/round2)\n\nThe prototype builds on your `model_validate(..., by_name=True)` approach. For custom initializers it re-keys **simple string validation aliases** before validation, unless the model already accepts names or disables alias validation. It keeps the stored payload unchanged, does not mutate model configuration, and still executes the custom initializer. The five direct cases from my earlier comment now pass. An additional seven controls pass, including extra fields, name-only validation, and AIMessage/ToolMessage/HumanMessage. The official checkpoint suite excluding unavailable Redis integration gives **252 passed** on current main `eb8ec111b3e9d3108af5d7bdcac51e3e913637a0`, Python 3.11.12 / Pydantic 2.12.5.\n\n**It is not a complete repair:** a custom-initialized aliased model nested inside a normal model still restores 42 as 1. The new boundary suite deliberately retains that failure: **7 passed, 1 failed**. General recursive aliases, unions, and arbitrary constructor transformations are not covered, so I would not propose merging this prototype as a general solution. The logs also retain an initial name-only-validation regression that the configuration guard fixed.\n\nWould you be interested in incorporating/adapting these tests into your existing PR, and deciding the reconstruction contract for nested custom initializers together? I can continue testing a revised candidate against these cases. I have not opened a competing PR; #9352 is still closed and unmerged pending maintainer assignment. Maintainer assignment of the existing author would preserve the current contribution path, if that is the desired scope.\n","createdAt":"2026-10-28T08:38:33Z","includesCreatedEdit":false,"isMinimized":false,"minimizedReason":"","reactionGroups":[],"url":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/pull/9352#issuecomment-6464473132","viewerDidAuthor":true}],"headRefOid":"b580e399e209bc3b7d6128c238acdb83fe120964","mergedAt":null,"reviews":[],"state":"CLOSED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-19T14:08:02Z","conclusion":"FAILURE","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/actions/runs/39266159062/job/118106160796","name":"check-issue-link","startedAt":"2026-10-19T14:07:51Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"Require Issue Link"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-19T14:09:10Z","conclusion":"CANCELLED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/actions/runs/39266130018/job/118106057775","name":"benchmark","startedAt":"2026-10-19T14:07:39Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"bench"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-10-19T14:07:46Z","conclusion":"SUCCESS","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/actions/runs/392